Short        : C-Net Pfile Graphic Maze Game like Pac-Man

Shareware Fee: None (Just send me E-Mail telling me if you like it or not.)
Creator      : DangerX
Author       : DangerX :)
Requirements : C-NET Amiga 3 or better, 14.4 Modem.
Email Address: danger@ctol.net
Web Address  : http://www.ctol.net/~danger/index.html
Aminet       : comm/cnet

GAME INTRO:

Your a little dude(ansi character) that goes around a maze, collecting
gold coins, while avoiding the poisonous spider.  The spider is fairly 
intelligent and will come after you.  Collect all the gold coins on a
level to advance to the next level.  Advancing levels also gains you
extra lives.(you start with 3).  Each coin collected is worth 1 point.
The goal??  Get the highest score you possibly can!

SOME NOTES:

Game saves Top-Ten Scores, Uses alot of Ansi Graphics.  Not recommended
for systems running at less than 14.4kbps(14.4 is the min. I would recommend
for playing the game..)  Users should have 80x23 Screens at a min.(if they 
have less, the graphics will become a mess!)

I've tested this remotely using Z-TERM on a Macintosh & ProComm95 on an IBM.
Both programs were able to view & play the game with no problems. 
HyperTerm(that cheap thing that comes with Win95...Really sucks for anything
ansi, really doesn't work well with this game.

MORE STUFF TO READ:

Should work on all OS Versions that can run C-NET Arexx Pfiles.
Tested on OS 3.1.  However, I really don't know as I don't run a C-NET
BBS.  I just like to write the games & stuff.


Originally I was going to have 2 spiders go after the player
but because I don't know C I was unable to get the program to run
fast enough..(It's slow enough with just one spider..)
so Insted of 2, I've made 1 SMART spider...which still keeps
it very challenging.

so I hope there's no bugs in it, if you find any, let me know via Internet
E-Mail.

INSTALLATION:
   
Create a Directory called "spiderlair" in your Pfiles: Area

example:

PFILES:spiderlair/

copy all the files into the PFILES:spiderlair/  folder.
The program will make the hi-score file, so you won't have to worry 
about making that or not having one.

ADDING SPIDER'S LAIR TO YOUR PFILES AREA:  

Adopt Orphan as an Arexx Pfile.  It should work
on multiple ports at the same time, but I'm unsure as I don't run a 
multi-port system, In Fact, I don't even run a C-Net BBS at this time.
I will be buying C-NET 4 in the very near future and will offer more
and better games at that time.  I do use commands that may cause slowing 
down on multi-port systems as well, So if you notice it slowing your BBS 
down to a crawl, you might want to remove this program from your system, 
or make it exclusive to one port at a time.

Disable More? Prompting

It can be made available to all age groups as it contains no adult
materials, or extreme violence.


